IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Civil Appeal No. 995 of 2021
CITATION: (2019) 4 SCC 17
YEAR: 2019

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: R.F. Nariman, Navin Sinha

PARTIES:
Swiss Ribbons vs Union of India

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code, 2016, Constitution of India

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 12A IBC, Section 29A IBC, Article 14

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
constitutionality of ibc, financial vs operational creditors, resolution over liquidation

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Upheld constitutional validity of Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code, affirming distinction between financial and operational creditors and primacy of resolution over recovery.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 12A IBC, Section 29A IBC, Article 14.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

